### Manual requests for the Lateral CMS service.
### Works with the Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client .http support.
### Paste the development passwords from src/Lateral.Cms/appsettings.Development.json below.
### (VS Code "REST Client" encodes `Basic user:password` for you; so does Visual Studio.)

@host = http://localhost:5080
@cmsUser = cms-ingest-svc
@cmsPassword = <Auth:Cms:Passwords[0]>
@userName = user@lateral.example
@userPassword = <Auth:Users[0].Password>
@adminName = admin@lateral.example
@adminPassword = <Auth:Users[1].Password>
@batchId = <batchId from a POST /cms/events response>

### 1. CMS pushes a batch: add, update, and a never-published unpublish.
### The service stores it and answers 202 (outcomes "queued") with a Location header; the worker applies it a
### moment later. Copy the batchId from the response into @batchId below, then run request 1b.
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUser}}:{{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish",   "id": "article-1", "version": 1, "payload": { "title": "Hello" },        "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z" },
  { "type": "publish",   "id": "article-1", "version": 2, "payload": { "title": "Hello again" },  "timestamp": "2024-01-02T00:00:00Z" },
  { "type": "unPublish", "id": "draft-7",   "version": 3, "payload": { "title": "Never live" },   "timestamp": "2024-01-03T00:00:00Z" },
  { "type": "delete",    "id": "article-9",                                                       "timestamp": "2024-01-04T00:00:00Z" }
]

### 1b. Follow the batch: queued, then completed with every event's final outcome (the CMS account or an admin may ask)
GET {{host}}/cms/batches/{{batchId}}
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUser}}:{{cmsPassword}}

### 2. Replaying it is harmless: older/identical events are reported as ignored
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUser}}:{{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "article-1", "version": 1, "payload": { "title": "Hello" }, "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z" }
]

### 3. A user sees only published, enabled entities
GET {{host}}/api/entities
Authorization: Basic {{userName}}:{{userPassword}}

### 4. An admin sees everything, with a status block
GET {{host}}/api/entities
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 5. One entity (404 for a user if it is hidden)
GET {{host}}/api/entities/draft-7
Authorization: Basic {{userName}}:{{userPassword}}

### 6. Admin hides an entity from users (local override, CMS unaffected)
POST {{host}}/api/entities/article-1/disable
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 7. ...and restores it
POST {{host}}/api/entities/article-1/enable
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 8. Paging
GET {{host}}/api/entities?limit=1
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 9. The wrong account is forbidden (CMS credentials cannot read)
GET {{host}}/api/entities
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUser}}:{{cmsPassword}}

### 10. No credentials: 401 with a Basic challenge
GET {{host}}/api/entities

### 10b. An admin checks the queue: batches waiting, age of the oldest, space used, failed batches
GET {{host}}/api/admin/ingestion
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 10c. An admin puts a failed batch back in the queue (409 if it has not failed)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/ingestion/{{batchId}}/requeue
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}

### 11. TEST ONLY: an admin erases everything, queued batches included, and starts again (Development only; 404 when switched off)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/reset
Authorization: Basic {{adminName}}:{{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "confirm": "reset-all-data" }
